#. failed to generate
msgid "Tipsy Patron"
msgstr "ほろ酔いかげんの客"

msgid "You see a tipsy individual who seems like they have something to say."
msgstr ""
"あなたはちょっと酔っているらしい人に気がついた。いいたいことがあるらしい。"

#. Allow plugins to modify the NPC priority of the POI generator NPC
msgid ""
"\"The other day I was arguing with a pilot about weird sensor readings in "
"the {sys} system. They claim that there has to be something there, but I "
"call bullocks!\""
msgstr ""
"｢このまえパイロットといいあいになってね。{sys}星系でセンサーが妙な結果をだし"
"たってことだった。そのパイロットはそこになにかあるにちがいないっていいはって"
"たけど、くそったれっていってやったよ！｣"

msgid ""
"\"Can you believe the audacity of some pilots? One was claiming they had "
"found some sort of anomaly in the {sys} system! Everyone knows that there is "
"nothing interesting left to find in space anymore! It's all explored!\""
msgstr ""
"｢一部のパイロットのあの厚かましさって信じられる？　{sys}星系で異常現象みたい"
"なのを見つけたなんていいはってたのもいたよ！　宇宙にはもう見つけてもおもしろ"
"いものなんてなにもないってみんな知ってるでしょ！　みんな探検されちゃったんだ"
"から！｣"

msgid ""
"\"The other day I was flying around the {sys} system and my system readings "
"spiked! I wasn't sure if it was a pirate or not, so I hauled my ass out of "
"there, but I still wonder what that could have been.\""
msgstr ""
"｢このまえ{sys}星系のあたりを飛んでてね、システムの測定結果に急な反応があった"
"んだ！　海賊だったのかどうかはわからなかったけど、さっさと尻を持ちあげて出"
"てったよ。でもまだなんだったんだろうって疑問に思うね｣"

msgid ""
"\"There's something funky about the {sys} system. I got some really weird "
"sensor readings there that I still don't know what to make of.\""
msgstr ""
"｢{sys}星系あたりになんか変わったものがあるね。あそこでほんとうに妙なセンサー"
"測定値が得られたんだよ。なんでそうなったのかまだわからないけど｣"

msgid "Inquire about the coordinates."
msgstr "座標についてたずねる。"

msgid "Be off."
msgstr "席を立つ。"

msgid ""
"After some persistence, you manage to get the coordinates of the weird "
"readings."
msgstr ""
"いくぶんしつこくいって、あなたはどうにかその妙な測定値が得られた座標を入手で"
"きた。"

#. failed to generate
msgid ""
"While boarding the ship, you manage to find some interesting data in the "
"navigation log. It looks like you may be able to follow the lead to "
"something of interest in the {sys} system. Do you wish to download the data?"
msgstr ""
"船に移乗して、あなたは興味深い情報が航法記録にあるのを発見した。{sys}星系にあ"
"る興味深いものに行きつけるかもしれない手がかりのようだ。この情報をダウンロー"
"ドしたいか？"

msgid ""
"While boarding the ship, you manage to find some interesting data in the "
"navigation log. It looks like you may be able to follow the lead to "
"something of interest in what appears to be a nearby system. Do you wish to "
"download the data?"
msgstr ""
"船に移乗して、あなたは興味深い情報が航法記録にあるのを発見した。近くの星系と"
"思われる場所にある興味深いものに行きつけるかもしれない手がかりのようだ。この"
"情報をダウンロードしたいか？"

msgid "Ignore."
msgstr "無視する。"

msgid "You ignore the information."
msgstr "あなたはこの情報を無視した。"

msgid "Ghost in the Mist"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A Frontier Liberation Front terrorist going by the moniker 'Ghost' is "
"rumored to have recovered some kind of strange ship from within the Nebula. "
"It is reported to be difficult to track on sensors. Find and deal with it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Disabled, the strange ship lies eerily silent. You and your boarding team "
"make your way through spartan cooridors to the bridge, encountering no "
"resistance. You find your target, Ghost, and a handful of injured crew "
"sheltering on the bridge. They drop their weapons and are quickly subdued."
msgstr ""

msgid "with some other terrorists"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ghost"
msgstr ""

msgid "Freedom is worth dying for!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Raising the Dead"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dvaered intelligence reports another FLF operative has been sighted deeper "
"into the nebula, in command of some kind of previously unseen battleship. We "
"don't know where they found it, but the Dvaered can not allow FLF terrorists "
"to possess this kind of technology."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This vessel seems designed for an atypically small crew for a battleship. "
"From an access terminal, a quick check of the ship's computer systems shows "
"that most of the surviving crew is sheltering in the medbay or armoury. Dim "
"emergency lighting guides your way through silent corridors to the bridge, "
"where you find your target lying injured and unconscious in the captain's "
"chair."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a terrorist fleet"
msgstr ""

msgid "Wraith"
msgstr "レイス"

msgid ""
"I'm so close to finding it! And once I do, we'll have the power to crush the "
"Dvaered and Empire alike!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Breaking Down the Graveyard Gate"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SECURITY CLASSIFICATION SECRET.\n"
"Empire intelligence has shared information with Dvaered High Command and "
"Astra Vigilis that a senior FLF military leader, codenamed Emerald Sword, "
"has located and recovered some kind of ancient superweapon from somewhere in "
"the depths of the Nebula. From what records the Empire has, it may have some "
"kind of {outfit}. Capture them alive for interrogation.\n"
"This will be a difficult battle, captain."
msgstr ""

msgid "nuclear based armament and autonomous drone fighter-bombers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The aesthetics of this battleship look like something from an ancient holo-"
"documentary, a relic from centuries ago. The bulkheads lie in sharp angles "
"and clean lines, and despite the damage from your battle, you can tell that "
"the ship was fully overhauled very recently and refurbished with more modern "
"systems. As you breach the vessel, you receive a communication from the "
"captain, who wishes to negotiate their surrender in exchange for more "
"lenient treatment of their crew. You take them into custody swiftly and "
"without incident."
msgstr ""

msgid "with an enormous terrorist fleet"
msgstr ""

msgid "Now witness the power of this fully armed and operational battleship!"
msgstr ""

#. Help support fleet survive Arandon. Also, they've apparently spent a little too long in the deep Nebula...
#. To be able to capture
msgid "The Baron's End"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Baron Sauterfeldt, the governor of the independent world Ulios in the Ingot "
"system, is wanted for trial by the Empire under suspicion of masterminding "
"theft from a Great House and trafficking in illegal Nebula artefacts. He is "
"known to be in command of a rare military model of pre-Incident destroyer "
"and is likely to be supported by larger vessels from the Ulios planetary "
"defense fleet."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cowed by your defeat of their fleet, the Baron's officers and crew stand "
"down. You've been aboard this ship before, and lead your boarding party "
"directly to Sauterfeldt's lavishly-appointed office. A low-yield detonation "
"charge blasts open the reinforced door, and you find the Baron whimpering "
"and cowering in the corner, holding a pile of his precious artefacts tightly "
"to his chest. Your crew drags him away in cuffs."
msgstr ""

msgid "supported by the Ulios planetary defense fleet"
msgstr ""

msgid "Baron Sauterfeldt"
msgstr "ザウターフェルト男爵"

msgid ""
"And here I thought we had a mutually beneficial relationship. Taking that "
"bounty was quite foolish, you know."
msgstr ""

#. Main force of Ulios planetary defense fleet
#. And some smaller than destroyer-size ships
#. Must have completed Baron Sauterfeldt missions & 1st two Shark campaign missions.
#. TODO rewrite dv_bikers so we don't need it as a prereq
msgid "Abominable Intelligence"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SECRET: An experimental wing of drone fightercraft have been misplaced, and "
"the Empire would like them destroyed quietly and without any fuss. Your "
"prompt attention to and silence on this matter is appreciated."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You open an access hatch on the drone. The interior is cramped with "
"equipment and a couple of spider-like maintenance bots which evidently shut "
"down when the ship was disabled, but the vessel does appear to have inactive "
"life support systems and an uncomfortable berth for a pilot. The cockpit has "
"an empty seat, with a spherical device affixed to the dash and wired into "
"all of the systems with a mess of cables. You unceremoniously rip it out. "
"Maybe the Empire wants it back."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your Astra Vigilis contact seems surprised when you drop a fist-sized "
"computer core in front of them."
msgstr ""

msgid "the target"
msgstr ""

msgid "with a few light drone escorts."
msgstr ""

msgid "IFF_ERR[37601]: PARAM UNDEFINED. HOSTILES DETECTED. ENGAGING."
msgstr ""

#. Only available pre-Collective plot. Serves as worldbuilding, Empire rep, and to guide players gently to finding it.
msgid "A Collective Conspiracy"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SECRET: A deserter is attempting to make off with a squadron of experimental "
"drone fighters. You are to proceed to Polack and destroy them. Once they are "
"dealt with, you will forget anything you know about the traitor or this "
"drone technology."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Most of the crew were injured in the battle, but a determined few still "
"resist, and your boarding party has a firefight halfway down the Pacifier's "
"main access corridor. You caught them in the open and swiftly dispatch the "
"remaining defenders, before blasting the bridge door open with a low-yield "
"detonator. Your target makes a show of dropping their service pistol, and "
"are taken into custody."
msgstr ""

msgid "Major Gray"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You're just a bump in the road, merc. Once we have the Collective under our "
"full control, the Emperor is next."
msgstr ""

#. Only available pre-Collective plot. Serves as worldbuilding, Empire rep, and to guide players gently to finding it.
msgid "Road to the Stars"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SECRET: A remnant of the Collective, a capital Drone Carrier mothership, has "
"stopped responding to control signals and instead has been travelling toward "
"an unknown destination. You are to intercept and destroy it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ship is pitch-black inside. Disabled maintenance dones, spider-like with "
"spindly limbs, lie collapsed in heaps or on their backs like dead bugs. You "
"cross a catwalk over silent machinery, and enter the bridge. In the centre "
"of the room is a large spherical device, with connectors and exhaust tubes "
"stretching haphazardly from it into ports on the walls, ceiling, and various "
"conventional computer systems. It clicks and whirrs at your approach, "
"several lights flashing with unknown meaning. A camera on the ceiling "
"swivels to track your movements. As your crew rips out the cables, the "
"lights die one by one, until the AI core lies dark and silent."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You unload the Drone Carrier's AI core on a cargo transport. The Astra "
"Vigilis representative hesitates, but marks the bounty as 'captured alive' "
"nonetheless."
msgstr ""

msgid "with an automated drone fleet."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"ERR.EER.ERr.eRr.S1gn@l R3c1ev3d. I aM n0t @l0ne. WARNING: OBSTACLES "
"DETECTED. DESTROY. DESTROY."
msgstr ""

#. Only available post-Collective plot. Serves as worldbuilding for Taomi.
#. On completion, add Drone Carrier and Heavy Drone Bay to Empire elite ships & outfits.
msgid "Flak and Frenzy"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Travellers entering Frontier space have been complaining of harassment and "
"shakedowns from a self-proclaimed 'warlord'. Capture him alive if possible."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ship's crew stand down as you breach the vessel. Lord Flakfinger "
"himself, young and arrogant, throws a punch but is quickly knocked down by "
"your crew. He scoffs as you cuff him. 'Auntie will have me out within a day.'"
msgstr ""

msgid "with small escort"
msgstr ""

msgid "Lord Flakfinger"
msgstr ""

msgid "You must be one of those Frontier weaklings, too!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Flak 2, Explosive Boogaloo"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Lord Flakfinger's rich aunt paid his bail, and he went right back to "
"shooting at Frontier merchant traffic, this time in a larger ship. Dead or "
"alive this time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This Retribution cruiser is brand new, straight out of the Dvaered "
"shipyards. Gleaming metal contrasts with battle damage from your weapons, "
"and the shouts and groans of injured crew fill the air. They're too busy "
"collecting their injured and trying to keep the ship intact to resist your "
"boarding party. You breach the bridge within minutes, where before he can "
"say a word, Lord Flakfinger is quickly subdued by a solid punch to the face. "
"He's dragged out uncerimoniously by your crew."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a hired fleet"
msgstr ""

msgid "You peasants will pay for what you did to me!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Wrath and Railguns"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Lord Flakfinger has been dealt with, but now his aunt, Lady Railfist, is out "
"for vengeance. Put a stop to this problem, once and for all."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your boarding party breaches into the battleship with an explosive charge, "
"and are met by an unpleasant surprise. A hail of minigun fire tears down the "
"corridor as you and your crew dive back into your ship. You hold tight while "
"one of your crew spacewalks up the hull, and plants another explosive on the "
"exterior, at your target's estimated location. When the dust clears, you "
"find your target and her retinue pinned under rubble and nursing their "
"injuries. You disarm and take them into custody without further incident."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a dangerous fleet"
msgstr ""

msgid "Lady Railfist"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fury and vengeance, wrath and flame! I will take everything from you, as you "
"took my nephew from me!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Intellectual Property"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"House Goddard, the shipyard responsible for the Goddard battleship and "
"related intellectual property, has asked us to apprehend one 'Norm "
"Alphurson', nominally there as a purchaser for an independent station. "
"Apparently he and his escort have been lingering around the Goddard "
"shipyards, taking suspicious deep scans of Goddard property."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As your boarding party prepares to breach into the corvette, your target "
"hails you with a frantic surrender. It seems they don't intend to put up a "
"fight, and are quickly taken into custody."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a small escort"
msgstr ""

msgid "Norm Alphurson"
msgstr ""

msgid "There's nothing wrong with just looking, is there?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stolen Blueprints"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"House Goddard has interrogated the spy you captured for them, and learned "
"that another foreign agent has just managed to breach Goddard systems and "
"has copied secure House Goddard blueprints for an unreleased technology in "
"development. It may not be too late to catch the spy. Kill them if necessary."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You breach the pirate ship and find the crew holding a gun to your target's "
"head. They offer to give him up in exchange for leniency. Well, that was "
"easy."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a small fleet"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shadowrunner"
msgstr ""

msgid "These prototype weapon plans are worth a lot to my buyer!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Weapons Free"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Foreign agents have stolen House Goddard's test platform, an old "
"demilitarized Goddard hull, which was currently loaded with experimental "
"weapons not yet available to the public. They have two jobs for you: First, "
"protect House Goddard intellectual property by preventing the escape of the "
"ship. Second: Assuming you survive, report back on how effective the weapons "
"were in a real firefight. If you die, they'll consider it a successful test."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fortunately this ship was manned with only the skeleton crew that stole it, "
"and most of them were injured in the battle. The disabled hulk is still an "
"impressive sight on the inside, and only a few crewmen are able to put up "
"minor resistance as you storm the bridge. Your target takes a shot to his "
"arm and drops his weapon, then is quickly subdued."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a sizable escort"
msgstr ""

msgid "Gunhead"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Just imagine these guns in every black market and on every Pirate Kestrel!"
msgstr ""

#. Doesn't block normal finishing
msgid "Conversion Therapy"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Sirius government has placed a bounty on a notorious smuggler who they "
"say is 'destabilizing the social fabric of the community'. They insist that "
"she be delivered alive for therapeutic intervention."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Haskins surrenders sullenly, posing no resistance as she's dragged to your "
"brig."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a few other undesirables"
msgstr ""

msgid "Free Trader Haskins"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Think for yourself, what they do to people isn't right! I won't let you take "
"me alive!"
msgstr ""

msgid "New Disciples"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Sirius government has placed a bounty on a pirate operating in the "
"southern reaches of Sirian space. We have been told that this pirate has "
"been 'leading the flock astray', and is to be delivered alive for re-"
"education."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The pirate crew take a few shots at your boarding party, but between their "
"injuries and the battle damage to their ship they pose little resistance. "
"You find Freejoy on the bridge, lying crumpled on the floor, injured but "
"alive."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a small band of pirates"
msgstr ""

msgid "Captain Freejoy"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"What's so wrong with a life of freedom? People should be able to do what "
"they please!"
msgstr ""

#. does not require conversion_1, either can be done in any order. Both will need to be complete for conversion_3
msgid "The Wandering Lamb"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Sirius government has placed an urgent bounty to capture a Dreamer Clan "
"pirate lord. We have been cautioned that they are known to manifest powerful "
"psychic abilities."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Of the pirate crew, those not injured from the battle seem to be delirious "
"or high on a number of substances. When your boarding party enters the "
"bridge, it's a truly strange sight: the room is dominated by a dance floor "
"in the centre, complete with a disco ball and pumping electronic music. The "
"captain herself is swaying and spinning with several of her crew, who don't "
"seem to notice as you cuff her and lead her away."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a sizable pirate crew"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dreamer Starheart"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"I was one of them once, now my wings are no longer clipped. I can see so "
"many colours in the astral."
msgstr ""

msgid "Nubulous Iconoclast"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Sirius government has placed a bounty on one Sister Brightstar, wanted "
"dead or alive for heretical teachings."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As you breach the vessel, the crew call out that they are unarmed and intend "
"to offer no resistance. You find Sister Brightstar sitting with several of "
"her disciples in the ship's meditation chamber. She says nothing as you "
"apprehend her."
msgstr ""

msgid "with her congregation"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sister Brightstar"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Sirichana is dead, and the Nebula is his corpse!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Alternative Medicine"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Soromid government has a poacher problem. Did you know there's wild "
"populations of feral bioships at the edge of Soromid space? It seems some "
"people believe that bioship organs have healing properties, and there's a "
"thriving black market trade in them. The Soromid want these poachers dead."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a few small escorts"
msgstr ""

msgid "Doc Goodstuff"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Look man, they're just animals! Nothing wrong with earning an honest living!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Wildlife Preservation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Soromid security has asked Astra Vigilis to help again with their ongoing "
"anti-poaching operations. A Kestrel has been spotted capturing live feral "
"bioship young. Take it out."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a moderate fleet of poachers"
msgstr ""

msgid "Zoomonger"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The money from those scientists is too good to pass up. You'll regret ever "
"seeing me here!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stop the Slaughter"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We've been given the last known location of one 'Doctor Slaughter', a Za'lek "
"renegade who appears to be behind the largest poaching operation in Soromid "
"space."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a posse of poachers"
msgstr ""

msgid "Doctor Slaughter"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Countless discoveries await locked inside these creatures' flesh and organs. "
"What could be more important than the advancement of knowledge?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Blazing in the Nebula"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A smuggler is operating around the edge of the Nebula near the border "
"between Empire and Soromid space. Normally this wouldn't be an issue, as a "
"healthy grey market keeps commerce moving. But in this case, they've been "
"dealing a new highly addictive and dangerous drug, and it's attracting too "
"much attention. Put a stop to it before the Empire is forced to crack down "
"on regional commerce."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your boarding party breaches into the cargo bay of the Clydesdale, finding "
"it full of pallet after pallet of narcotics. Making your way carefully down "
"the length of the disabled ship, a few of the uninjured crew take potshots "
"at you, but are quickly overwhelmed and disarmed. The door to the bridge is "
"sealed and bolted, but a small demolition charge swiftly takes care of that "
"problem, and within moments of entry, the notorious drug runner Eisenberg is "
"cuffed and on his way to your brig."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a moderate escort gang."
msgstr ""

msgid "Eisenburg"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You're too close to the source, soul. Can't have you ruining a good thing "
"here."
msgstr ""

msgid "Never Bring an AI to a Battleship Fight"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A prototype automated Za'lek capital battlegroup has been hacked and "
"hijacked by anti-AI radicals. The danger that it poses is immense. The "
"Za'lek government wants it destroyed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ship is completely empty, but shows sign of intrusion everywhere. "
"Bulkheads had been hastily removed, wires and cables patched, moved, and "
"reorganized, and computer systems' casing opened. You find the bridge empty "
"and silent, but a member of your crew investigating the science lab finds an "
"enormous computer core spliced into the ship systems. You disconnect it and "
"haul it back to your ship."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You unload the R.A.T.'s AI core on a cargo transport. The Astra Vigilis "
"representative hesitates, but marks the bounty as 'captured alive' "
"nonetheless. Maybe the Za'lek will appreciate that you've returned their "
"hardware."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a prototype automated fleet and several hijackers"
msgstr ""

msgid "AUTONOMOUS R.A.T. PROTO-001"
msgstr ""

#. very good synergy with the RAT, not something to pass up on
msgid ""
"[ERR-7F3A] IFF_TABLE_CORRUPT :: CORE_AI_REVERT FOUND TEMPLATE 'DESTROY-ALL-"
"HUMANS'"
msgstr ""

msgid "AWOL Lab Partner"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A university graduate student has put a bounty out on their lab partner, who "
"vanished in the middle of their thesis project on modular fuel synethesis "
"dynamics. Bring her back alive, please."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your target is an unarmed student, and she offers no resistance as you "
"apprehend her."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sarah grumbles and glares at you as you turn her over to her lab partner."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a small group of shady pirates"
msgstr ""

msgid "Graduate Student Sarah"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hey, this was an important business meeting!"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Stolen Prototype"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Two students were working on a modular prototype ramscoop as their graduate "
"thesis project. One of them stole it, and is believed to be trying to fence "
"it on the black market. Za'lek authorities don't care about the renegade "
"student or the prototype: they just don't want the Black Lotus Clan to have "
"it. Crash the sale and blast everyone out of the sky."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Though perhaps officially a pirate now, having sold stolen technology, Sarah "
"isn't any better armed than before. The crew she hired on for her ship "
"likewise don't want to get killed, and offer no resistance. You take Sarah "
"into custody without incident."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As Sarah is led away, it seems to hit her that this time she's probably "
"going to prison."
msgstr ""

msgid "with a group of pirates"
msgstr ""

msgid "Too late, I've already been paid! Screw academia, I'm set for life now!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Buyer's Remorse"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Za'lek intelligence has located the stolen {outfit} in the possession of a "
"Black Lotus crime lord. Za'lek authorities don't care about the final "
"disposition of the prototype, but this contract stipulates that it not be "
"left in pirate hands."
msgstr ""

msgid "prototype modular ramscoop"
msgstr ""

msgid "with a dangerous pirate fleet"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Kingpin"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This is my prize now, and you're only getting it over my dead body. Or, "
"preferably, yours."
msgstr ""

#. Don't allow earning the prototype ramscoop until Chapter 1.
msgid "One Goatee to Rule them All"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A pirate warlord known as Rainbow Goatee is planning a large scale revenge "
"raid after his disciples were defeated. Seeing this as a major threat, "
"several guilds of the Space Trader's Society have funded a large bounty to "
"neutralize the upcoming menace."
msgstr ""

msgid "with heavy support"
msgstr ""

msgid "Rainbow Goatee"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Goatees shall never be forgotten!"
msgstr ""

#. So the escorts are actually all the previous goatees + the new boss
#. Have the rest be smaller than the starbridge so there's a bit of weird cruft there
#. Have to defeat all the goatees first
msgid "Executing the Executioner"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SECURITY CLASSIFICATION SECRET.\n"
"The Astra Vigilis has received an exceptional order to eliminate a renegade "
"Executioner. Target is flying an Empire Peacemaker and is expected to be "
"extremely dangerous. The target is equipped with an experimental {outfit}. "
"Proceed with caution."
msgstr ""

msgid "shield aura generator"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alarms blare in the corridors of this once-mighty Peacemaker, and the "
"hissing of damaged systems and shouts of injured crew echo down the halls. "
"Your boarding party quickly and professionally makes its way to the bridge, "
"encountering only minor resistance from the dazed crew, who are quickly "
"subdued. Blasting the secured bridge hatch open with a low-yield detonator, "
"you find that the captain's console had exploded when overloaded, and your "
"target lies injured and unconscious. The remaining uninjured crew surrender "
"as you drag Executor Sable back to your ship."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A surprisingly large contingent of Empire soldiers meet you at the landing "
"pad, where they take Sable into custody."
msgstr ""

msgid "with support"
msgstr ""

msgid "Executor Sable"
msgstr ""

msgid "It seems like the Empire can't even do the dirty work itself."
msgstr ""

#. To control whether or not the player did it
msgid "A Bark in the Dark"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An ex-Astra Vigilis guild member known as Hellhound has gone rogue after "
"collusion with a high priority bounty target. They are flying the Hellhound "
"and believed to be accompanied by other rogue members. The Astra Vigilis "
"wants them captured alive."
msgstr ""

msgid "with heavy escorts"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hellhound"
msgstr ""

msgid "What? Astra Vigilis sticking bounty hunters on me?"
msgstr ""

msgid "To Hell and Back"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ex-Astra Vigilis guild member Hellhound has escaped their confinement "
"and are once again on the loose. The Astra Vigilis needs them captured alive "
"again."
msgstr ""

msgid "with heavier escorts"
msgstr ""

msgid "You again!?"
msgstr ""

